00:00:01.360 --> 00:00:06.640
Hi, my name is Don Cole. I'm a PhD

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:09.440
student in the ISC department NC State

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:11.840
University. My research focus on

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:14.160
building a realtime decision support

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:16.080
framework for additive manufacturing

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:18.800
using a diffusion model which is one of

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:21.199
the core algorithm of generative AI.

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:23.920
Laser powder bed fusion is not only for

00:00:21.199 --> 00:00:25.680
prototyping but also producing rear

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:28.240
parts in many applications like

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:30.000
aerospace and medical. But the process

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:32.480
is highly sensitive to parameter

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.559
settings. So even small deviation from

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:37.120
the optimal setting can cause serious

00:00:34.559 --> 00:00:39.360
quality problem and defects may still

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:42.559
occur even on the optimal setting as

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:44.320
defect formation is some stochastic. My

00:00:42.559 --> 00:00:46.239
work goes one step further from the

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:48.719
previous studies not only to predict

00:00:46.239 --> 00:00:50.879
what may happen next but also to support

00:00:48.719 --> 00:00:52.879
the real time decision on whether the

00:00:50.879 --> 00:00:55.840
ongoing printing process should continue

00:00:52.879 --> 00:00:59.520
or stop. For this I used the paragan

00:00:55.840 --> 00:01:02.000
data set released by okage in 2023 which

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:04.879
contains multimodel information aligned

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:07.200
across space and time including postmelt

00:01:04.879 --> 00:01:09.680
post record images in sich environmental

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:12.080
signals and so on. What I need to

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:13.760
generate is a postmelt images and other

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:16.640
modalities are being used as a

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:18.479
conditioner information. I propose a

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:20.320
framework consisting of three

00:01:18.479 --> 00:01:23.600
components. The first piece is

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:26.080
generator. It is a diffusion model that

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:28.960
forecast the next layer postmelt images

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:31.920
based on previous object layer. The

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:34.159
second piece is evaluator a CNN based

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:36.000
defect predictor that takes generated

00:01:34.159 --> 00:01:38.560
output and predict the corresponding

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:40.799
defect rate. The last piece is the

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:43.360
decision engine which use the predicted

00:01:40.799 --> 00:01:45.840
defect distribution to make go or no

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:48.799
decision in real time. Based on this

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:51.280
setup, I can generate multiple layer uh

00:01:48.799 --> 00:01:53.040
samples, evaluate each of them, and

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:55.920
finally estimate the defect

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:58.880
distribution. Now, it allows me to make

00:01:55.920 --> 00:02:01.600
answer the aware decisions. The result

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:03.920
show that my model generate high quality

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:06.000
samples with structure and texture close

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:08.239
to the ground truth. And since the

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:10.399
evaluator estimate defect rate for

00:02:08.239 --> 00:02:12.959
different classes of defect, the

00:02:10.399 --> 00:02:16.160
framework can now flag risky regions

00:02:12.959 --> 00:02:18.400
based on a userdefined threshold.

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:22.720
This figure show the defect distribution

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:24.959
of class 2 3 and 11 at layer number 100.

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:27.280
In this example, if the 100 real

00:02:24.959 --> 00:02:28.879
printing yields a second class defect of

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:31.040
0.230,

00:02:28.879 --> 00:02:33.040
then it suggests to stop the printing as

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:35.040
this defect will be propagated and make

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:37.440
the process worse.

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:40.480
My work is a unified framework for

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:43.200
real-time riskaware LPBF monitoring by

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:45.200
using generative AI and also even the

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:48.239
first diffusion model built upon the

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:50.319
paragraph data set. In the future I want

00:02:48.239 --> 00:02:53.360
to improve the generalization across

00:02:50.319 --> 00:02:56.560
different build machine and connect all

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:58.560
the uh forecast to the finer part

00:02:56.560 --> 00:03:01.200
quality. Thanks for your time and

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:01.200
support.


